From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fedora SL7 Remix contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: limit rfkill workaround to Romulus

The Romulus firmware advertises RFKill support, but configuring it prevents
ath12k enumeration on Surface Laptop 7. The original downstream workaround
returned early for every ath12k device. Preserve the required behavior only
when the root device tree identifies one of the two supported Romulus models.

Based-on: https://github.com/ProgrammerIn-wonderland/ELLX-Kernel/commit/2e8c2d99262435510fb9b1f48f4637a4b9149099
Signed-off-by: Fedora SL7 Remix contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -76,6 +76,10 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (!(ab->target_caps.sys_cap_info & WMI_SYS_CAP_INFO_RFKILL))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,romulus13") ||
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,romulus15"))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
 
-- 
